Review round 1 (independent reviewer, verdict CHANGES-REQUIRED):

F1 MAJOR — fixed: Workspace built `source` as an inline literal, so note
edits rebuilt the ExportController and silently reset findings to "all"
(a deselected finding's text would re-enter the next download). Fix:
controller carries `sourceReportId`; the panel restores the previous
request via `restoreRequest` (sanitized to availability/finding ids) when
the sealed report identity is unchanged, resets on a different report.
New spec leg covers it.

F2 MINOR — fixed: a note on a deselected finding was pruned with no
note-level line. Controller now counts `notesExcludedWithFindings` and
the panel discloses "N note(s) excluded with their deselected findings."

F3 MINOR — run.json predated the committed spec layout; the registered
command is re-run on the fix commit below, refreshing the record.

F4 NIT — removed redundant `await context.close()` from the spec.

F5 NIT — added "Notes" count row to the preview grid.

F6 NIT/a11y — notes controls nest inside role="option" (pre-existing
pattern shared with AlignmentDetail); flagged for T37, not expanded here.

